On Jan 8, 12:52=A0am, Patric Mueller <bh...@bigfoot.com> wrote:

> I doubt that NAOs patch will work on a Windows machine.

At least one of the patches on there (that I wrote) definitely won't
work on Windows. It replaces the lockfile mechanism with a fcntl()
mechanism, to get rid of the problematic extraneous lockfile issues
that I ran into more or less weekly before this patch.

There is a possibility that in a bad disconnect a lockfile can be left
around in the vanilla sources, resulting in someone having to go
manually delete it before anyone else can start the game. My fcntl()
patch fixes this unconditionally, but was written in a very Linux
specific manner.

Most people wouldn't run into this on a standalone system, but at a
few hundred games per day (and always on a remote server) it cropped
up regularly on NAO.

